## Reading it yourself

To pretty-print any of it, paste the script into your browser console, or use a formatter. From a
terminal:

```bash
npx js-beautify --indent-size 2 yourfile.html
```

Two things worth knowing if you want to satisfy yourself nothing odd is in there:

* **The only external addresses in the whole file** are `cdnjs.cloudflare.com` (the Leaflet mapping
  library) and `cartodb-basemaps-*` (the grey street tiles behind the districts). You can confirm with
  `grep -o 'https\?://[a-z.-]*' index.html | sort -u`.
* **The code makes no network requests of its own and stores nothing.** There is no `fetch(`, no
  `XMLHttpRequest`, no `eval(`, no `new Function`, no `localStorage`, no cookies — I checked all of them
  and every count is zero. `atob()` (the Base64 decoder) appears only in the outer file, only in
  `b64ToStr()`, and only ever reads from the `MAPS` object already inside the file. Once the page has
  loaded Leaflet and the map tiles, everything happens locally in your browser.

The one thing that *is* used is `innerHTML`, six or seven times, to write the legend and results panels
from your own election numbers.
